  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sunil Uraon And 3 Others vs State Of U.P. on 22 August, 2019 Author: Siddharth Bench: Siddharth High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Court No. - 78 Case :- Criminal Misc. Bail Application No. - 34201 of 2019 Applicant :- Sunil Uraon And 3 Others Opposite Party :- State Of U.P. Counsel for Applicant :- Ashok Kumar Mishra,Nagendra Kumar Singh Counsel for Opposite Party :- G.A. Hon'ble Siddharth,J.",
    "facts": "The instant bail application has been filed on behalf of the applicants, Sunil Uraon, Mohan Uraon, Suraj Mahto and Bablu Kachhap, with a prayer to release them on bail in Case Crime No.113 of 2019, under Sections 272, 273, 120-B IPC and Section 60 Excise Act, Police Station Karanda, District- Ghazipur, during pendency of trial. Submission is that the applicants have been implicated under Section 272 and 273 IPC despite existence of Food Safety and Standards Act Act in this regard. The offence under Section 60 of Excise Act is bailable offence and triable by Magistrate. The applicants are alleged to have falsely implicated. The applicants do not have any criminal history to their credit. The applicants are languishing in jail since 03.7.2019. In case, the applicants are released on bail, they will not misuse Sunil Uraon And 3 Others vs State Of U.P. on 22 August, 2019 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/22836505/ 1 the liberty of bail.",
    "arguments": "Per contra learned A.G.A. has opposed the bail prayer of the applicants by contending that the innocence of the applicants cannot be adjudged at pre trial stage, therefore, they do not deserves any indulgence. In case the applicants are released on bail they will again indulge in similar activities and will misuse the liberty of bail.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Per contra learned A.G.A. has opposed the bail prayer of the applicants by contending that the innocence of the applicants cannot be adjudged at pre trial stage, therefore, they do not deserves any indulgence.",
    "respondent_arguments": "In case the applicants are released on bail they will again indulge in similar activities and will misuse the liberty of bail.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
